Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Findings of the 2026-10-20 audit (A gasto, B ingesta/tiempo, C indicadores), fixed in the fork's own code:

- One "today": FoodDays.today() is the meal day (04:00 roll, upstream's logical day) everywhere the fork
  says today: the Today and Food cards, the history, the day chips, the coach's TODAY/FOOD LOG/balance,
  the meal marks and the week. A dinner logged at 00:45 is on the day Today still shows.
- Week: last week is reviewed (and shown, also to the coach) from 10:00 on the new week's first day, so the
  late Sunday dinner, its mark and the strap's morning hand-over are in; the review sees every workout the
  coach and the Workouts list see (Health Connect, files, lifting apps, detected); weeks start on the
  locale's first day like the Food history and «Mi día».
- Coach: what was eaten today (foods per meal, cut at 120 chars) and the previous days' P/C/F averages;
  steps in the Today card's order (strap first); NIGHTS takes the day's main sleep, never a nap.
- Food card: no "if you eat nothing more, a deficit of…" with nothing logged; the burn reloads when the
  strap syncs, a Health Connect import ends or a workout is analysed (Today, Food, history, «Tu gasto real»).
- Meal marks: the prompt says how much of the served portion was eaten; a corrected food name or macros
  asks for a new mark (marks stored before keep showing); one English name per meal type in every prompt.
- Moving a meal to another day keeps a 01:30 dinner in the small hours of its new day.
- Health Connect refresh: a failed active-calories read no longer leaves the activity inside the basal
  (phone total counted the activity twice).
- Workouts analysed on under 20 heart-rate samples are re-checked for 14 days (a strap that synced late).
- Repair pass: a logged day whose calories_in in the nutrition lane was lost or replaced is rewritten;
  CSV days without photos are never touched.
- Profile, scale and goals lines for the meal marks, the week and the workout estimate come from one
  helper (VictorPersonLines), with the coach's consent inside.

No data model changes: no new JSON fields, no Room changes, nothing deleted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
